---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import WidgetWrapper from '~/components/ui/WidgetWrapper.astro';
import Headline from '~/components/ui/Headline.astro';
import FAQs from '~/components/widgets/FAQs.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'How Roof Insurance Claims Work in Hawaii | R&C Roofing',
  description:
    'Learn how the roof insurance claim process works in Hawaii and where R&C Roofing can help with inspections, damage documentation, roofing scopes, and repairs.',
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>

  <!-- P-01 Hero — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="py-8 md:py-12 max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-[42px] md:text-[56px] font-medium leading-[115%] tracking-tighter font-heading mb-6">
        How the Roof Insurance Claim Process Works in Hawaii
      </h1>
      <p class="block text-[20px] md:text-[24px] font-medium font-heading text-heading mb-6 leading-[130%] tracking-tight">
        Know What to Expect After Roof Damage
      </p>
      <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-4 mb-8">
        <p>If your roof has been damaged by severe weather or another event, the insurance process can involve several steps before repair work begins.</p>
        <p>Your insurance carrier handles the claim and determines coverage. Your roofing contractor evaluates the roof and provides information about the work that may be needed.</p>
        <p>R&amp;C Roofing Contractors helps with the roofing side of that process. We inspect accessible roof areas, document relevant findings, provide contractor-side scope information when appropriate, and complete roofing work if the project moves forward.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Schedule a Roof Damage Inspection</a>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-white dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Who Handles What — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <Headline title="Who Handles What During a Roof Insurance Claim?" classes={{ container: 'mb-4 md:mb-6' }} />
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-8 md:mb-12">
      Understanding each party’s role can make the process easier to follow.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-6">
        <h3 class="text-[18px] md:text-[20px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-4">You and Your Insurance Carrier</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">—</span>Review your policy and claim requirements</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">—</span>File and manage the insurance claim</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">—</span>Determine whether the loss is covered</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">—</span>Determine the amount payable under the policy</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 mt-0.5">—</span>Handle claim decisions and settlement questions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-6">
        <h3 class="text-[18px] md:text-[20px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-4">R&amp;C Roofing Contractors</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 text-green-600 mt-0.5">✓</span>Inspect accessible roofing areas</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 text-green-600 mt-0.5">✓</span>Document relevant visible roof conditions</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 text-green-600 mt-0.5">✓</span>Explain the roofing work we recommend</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 text-green-600 mt-0.5">✓</span>Provide a roofing estimate or scope when appropriate</li>
          <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="shrink-0 text-green-600 mt-0.5">✓</span>Complete the roofing work if the project moves forward</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted italic">
      R&amp;C is a licensed Hawaii roofing contractor, License C-33642. We are not a public adjuster and do not negotiate insurance settlements or determine coverage.
    </p>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-900/30"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Step 1 — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="flex gap-5 mb-6">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[16px] text-white dark:text-slate-900">1</div>
      <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading">
        Document the Damage and Protect the Property
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
      <p>Once it is safe to do so, take photos or videos of visible damage.</p>
      <p>That may include roofing materials on the ground, interior ceiling stains, active water intrusion, or other changes you noticed after the event.</p>
      <p>If water is entering the property, take reasonable steps to prevent additional interior damage. Keep receipts for materials or services used to protect the property.</p>
      <p>Avoid climbing onto a wet or damaged roof yourself.</p>
      <p>Permanent roofing repairs generally should wait until the damage has been inspected or your insurer has authorized the work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-800 p-5">
      <p class="text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Where R&amp;C Can Help:</span> If you need a closer assessment of the roof, R&amp;C can inspect accessible roofing areas and document relevant visible conditions.
      </p>
      <a href="/roof-inspections/storm-and-wind-damage-inspection" class="inline-block mt-3 text-primary font-medium text-[14px] md:text-[15px] hover:underline">View Storm &amp; Wind Damage Inspections →</a>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-white dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Step 2 — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="flex gap-5 mb-6">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[16px] text-white dark:text-slate-900">2</div>
      <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading">
        Review Your Policy and Contact Your Insurance Carrier
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
      <p>Review your policy's claim procedures and contact your insurance company or agent to report the damage.</p>
      <p>Your carrier can tell you what information it needs, how the claim will be handled, and what deadlines apply to your policy.</p>
      <p>Provide factual information about what happened and the damage you observed. If your carrier asks for forms or additional documentation, follow its claim instructions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg border bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-5">
      <p class="text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
        <span class="font-semibold text-heading">Where R&amp;C Can Help:</span> R&amp;C can provide roofing-specific documentation when appropriate, including photos of relevant findings and information about the roofing work we recommend.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
        R&amp;C does not interpret insurance coverage or advise you on what your policy should pay.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-900/30"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Step 3 — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="flex gap-5 mb-6">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[16px] text-white dark:text-slate-900">3</div>
      <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading">
        The Roof and Claim Are Evaluated
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5 mb-8">
      <p>Your insurance carrier may assign an adjuster to inspect the property as part of its claim review.</p>
      <p>The adjuster evaluates the loss for the insurance company. R&amp;C evaluates the roofing system as a contractor.</p>
      <p>These are different roles.</p>
    </div>
    <h3 class="text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-3">What R&amp;C Evaluates</h3>
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted mb-5">Depending on the property and inspection conditions, we may look at:</p>
    <ul class="space-y-2 mb-8">
      {[
        'Roofing materials in affected areas',
        'Flashing and roof penetrations',
        'Visible attachment or fastener concerns',
        'Roof edges and drainage areas',
        'Signs of impact or displacement',
        'Other visible conditions relevant to the roofing scope',
      ].map((item) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
          <span class="shrink-0 text-primary mt-0.5">—</span>
          {item}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
      Our team includes HAAG Certified Inspector Robert Pilato, Certification #201408313, with specialized training in roof damage assessment.
    </p>
    <a href="/roof-inspections/haag-certified-inspection" class="inline-block mt-4 text-primary font-medium text-[14px] md:text-[15px] hover:underline">Learn About HAAG Certified Roof Inspections →</a>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-white dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Step 4 — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="flex gap-5 mb-6">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[16px] text-white dark:text-slate-900">4</div>
      <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading">
        Review the Carrier's Decision and the Roofing Scope
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5 mb-8">
      <p>After reviewing the claim, your insurance carrier will provide information about its decision and any covered work or payment.</p>
      <p>Read those documents carefully.</p>
      <p>R&amp;C can separately explain the roofing work we believe is appropriate based on the condition of the roof.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-6">
        <h3 class="text-[18px] md:text-[20px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-3">If the Scopes Match</h3>
        <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">If the carrier's approved scope and the roofing work being proposed align, the project can move toward scheduling once the necessary approvals and project details are in place.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-6">
        <h3 class="text-[18px] md:text-[20px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-3">If the Scopes Differ</h3>
        <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted mb-3">There may be situations where R&amp;C recommends work that is not reflected in the carrier's initial scope. When appropriate, we can provide additional contractor-side documentation explaining our roofing recommendation.</p>
        <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted mb-3">The insurance carrier determines whether additional work or cost will be covered.</p>
        <a href="/insurance-claim-help/denied-or-underpaid-claims" class="text-primary font-medium text-[14px] md:text-[15px] hover:underline">Learn About Denied or Underpaid Roof Claims →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-900/30"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Step 5 — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="flex gap-5 mb-6">
      <div class="shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-primary flex items-center justify-center font-heading font-medium text-[16px] text-white dark:text-slate-900">5</div>
      <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading">
        Complete the Roofing Work
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
      <p>Once the project is ready to move forward, R&amp;C can complete the agreed roof repair or replacement.</p>
      <p>As the roofing contractor, our responsibility is to perform the project according to the approved contract and applicable project requirements.</p>
      <p>Keep copies of roofing contracts, invoices, receipts, and other project documents. Your carrier may request documentation during or after the repair process.</p>
      <p>If additional roofing conditions are discovered after work begins, contact your carrier and follow its instructions before assuming that additional work will be covered.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <a href="/services/roof-replacement-and-new-installation" class="btn-primary">Explore Roof Repair and Replacement Services</a>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-white dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- Documents to Keep — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <Headline title="What Documents Should You Keep During the Claim?" classes={{ container: 'mb-4 md:mb-6' }} />
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted mb-4">
      Keeping your claim and roofing records together can make it easier to follow what has happened throughout the process.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted mb-6">Useful records may include:</p>
    <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
      {[
        'Photos and videos taken after the damage',
        'Your claim number',
        'Written communication from the carrier',
        'Carrier estimates or scope documents',
        'R&C inspection documentation',
        'Contractor estimates',
        'Signed roofing contracts',
        'Receipts for temporary protective measures',
        'Final invoices and project records',
      ].map((item) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3 text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted">
          <span class="shrink-0 text-primary mt-0.5">—</span>
          {item}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted italic">
      Your insurance carrier can tell you which documents it specifically requires.
    </p>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-900/30"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- What If Additional Damage Is Found — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading mb-8 md:mb-10">
      What If Additional Damage Is Found?
    </h2>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
      <p>Sometimes additional roofing conditions become visible only after work begins or materials are removed.</p>
      <p>If that happens, the next step depends on the project and your insurance claim.</p>
      <p>R&amp;C can document the roofing condition and explain any additional work we believe is needed. You should also contact your carrier and follow its process for reviewing work that was not included in the original claim scope.</p>
      <p>Do not assume additional work will automatically be covered.</p>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-white dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- What If Claim Is Denied — grey -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading mb-8 md:mb-10">
      What If Your Claim Is Denied or the Approved Scope Seems Incomplete?
    </h2>
    <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted space-y-5">
      <p>Start by reviewing the carrier's written explanation.</p>
      <p>If you still have questions about the physical condition of the roof, R&amp;C can provide a roof inspection and additional contractor-side information about visible findings and the work we recommend.</p>
      <p>R&amp;C cannot overturn a denial or negotiate a settlement on your behalf.</p>
      <p>If you need help with a coverage dispute, policy interpretation, or claim settlement issue, contact your insurance carrier, the Hawai&#699;i Insurance Division, or an appropriately licensed insurance professional.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <a href="/insurance-claim-help/denied-or-underpaid-claims" class="btn-primary">Learn About Denied or Underpaid Roof Claims</a>
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-slate-900/30"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- P-05 Resource Cards — white -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <Headline title="Explore Our Insurance Claim Resources" />
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 md:gap-8">
      {[
        {
          title: 'Roof Insurance Claim Help',
          description: 'Understand what R&C can provide during the roofing portion of an insurance claim.',
          href: '/insurance-claim-help',
          linkText: 'View Insurance Claim Help →',
        },
        {
          title: 'Denied or Underpaid Roof Claims',
          description: "Learn what to review when a claim is denied or the carrier's scope differs from the roofing work being recommended.",
          href: '/insurance-claim-help/denied-or-underpaid-claims',
          linkText: 'Learn About Claim Decisions →',
        },
        {
          title: 'Storm & Wind Damage Inspections',
          description: 'Have visible roof conditions evaluated after strong winds or severe weather.',
          href: '/roof-inspections/storm-and-wind-damage-inspection',
          linkText: 'View Storm Damage Inspections →',
        },
      ].map(({ title, description, href, linkText }) => (
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-white/16 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-card p-6 flex flex-col intersect-once intersect-quarter motion-safe:md:opacity-0 motion-safe:md:intersect:animate-fade">
          <h3 class="text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium font-heading leading-[130%] mb-3">{title}</h3>
          <p class="text-[14px] md:text-[15px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted mb-4 flex-1">{description}</p>
          <a href={href} class="text-primary font-medium text-[14px] md:text-[15px] hover:underline mt-auto">{linkText}</a>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-white dark:bg-transparent"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </WidgetWrapper>

  <!-- P-10 FAQs -->
  <FAQs
    title="Frequently Asked Questions"
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Should I call my insurance carrier before scheduling a roof inspection?',
        description:
          "You should follow the claim procedures in your policy and report damage within any deadlines that apply. You can also contact R&C when you need a roofing-specific assessment of the property.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Should I repair my roof before the insurance adjuster sees it?',
        description:
          "Take reasonable steps to protect the property from additional damage, but permanent repairs generally should wait until the damage has been inspected or your insurer has approved the work. Follow your carrier's instructions for your specific claim.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Does R&C meet with insurance adjusters?',
        description:
          "Availability and involvement can depend on the project and claim. R&C can provide contractor-side roofing information when appropriate. Confirm with our team what support is available for your specific situation.",
      },
      {
        title: 'How long does a roof insurance claim take?',
        description:
          "There is no single timeline. The process can depend on the carrier, the extent of the damage, inspection scheduling, documentation requests, and other claim-specific factors.",
      },
      {
        title: 'What is an insurance supplement?',
        description:
          "Additional damage or costs may sometimes be identified after an initial estimate is prepared. Your carrier will determine whether and how it handles additional documentation or changes to the claim.<br><br>R&C can provide contractor-side information about roofing conditions or additional work when appropriate.",
      },
      {
        title: 'What if my claim is denied?',
        description:
          "Review the carrier's written explanation first. R&C can inspect the roof and provide additional contractor-side documentation, but we do not overturn coverage decisions or negotiate claim disputes.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Who decides how much the insurance company will pay?',
        description:
          "The insurance carrier determines coverage and claim payment under the policy. R&C provides information about the roofing work and project cost as the contractor.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Can R&C complete the roofing work after the claim?',
        description:
          "Yes. R&C Roofing Contractors is a licensed Hawaii roofing contractor, License C-33642. If the project moves forward, our team can complete the agreed roof repair or replacement.",
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- P-12 Final CTA -->
  <WidgetWrapper containerClass="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
    <div class="w-full p-8 md:p-12 rounded-md shadow-xl dark:shadow-none dark:border dark:border-slate-600">
      <div class="text-center mb-8 md:mb-10">
        <h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-normal leading-[120%] tracking-tighter font-heading text-heading mb-4">
          Need Help With the Roofing Side of Your Claim?
        </h2>
        <div class="text-[16px] md:text-[17px] font-medium leading-[160%] text-muted dark:text-slate-400 space-y-3">
          <p>If your roof has been damaged, R&amp;C can help you understand the condition of the roofing system and the work that may be needed.</p>
          <p>We can inspect accessible roof areas, document relevant findings, and provide contractor-side information as your insurance claim moves forward.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-6 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 pt-8">
        <div class="text-[15px] md:text-[16px] font-medium leading-[180%] text-muted dark:text-slate-400">
          <p class="font-semibold text-heading text-[16px] md:text-[17px]">R&amp;C Roofing Contractors</p>
          <p>3302 Campbell Ave, Honolulu, HI 96815</p>
          <p>(808) 888-2524</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] md:text-[14px] italic">After-hours roofing concern? Use the online chat to contact the team.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary shrink-0">Schedule a Roof Damage Inspection</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </WidgetWrapper>

</Layout>
